Adds the Stellux nvkmd's dev, mem and va over /dev/gpuN. A dev is one GPU
context with two address heaps that split the GPU's user range at 2^38, a mem
is one buffer mapped whole on the GPU at a range of its own, and a va is a
range whose binds map buffers into the context. The pdev creates devs,
refuses a GPU whose user range is not [4 KiB, 2^39) and offers fixed maps
and overmaps. A dev creates no ctx (an nvkmd's object that submits work), so
vkCreateDevice fails at NVK's upload queue for any device with queues.

--- a/src/nouveau/vulkan/meson.build
+++ b/src/nouveau/vulkan/meson.build
@@ -162,7 +162,10 @@ if with_nouveau_stellux
   nvk_flags += '-DNVK_STELLUX'
   nvk_files += files(
     'nvkmd/stellux/nvkmd_stellux.h',
+    'nvkmd/stellux/nvkmd_stellux_dev.c',
+    'nvkmd/stellux/nvkmd_stellux_mem.c',
     'nvkmd/stellux/nvkmd_stellux_pdev.c',
+    'nvkmd/stellux/nvkmd_stellux_va.c',
   )
 endif
 
